#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Phase 448: CLAUDE.md -- the log row.
import sys, re
p = sys.argv[1]; s = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()
ROW = """| 448 | 2026-10-12 | **QA sweep: tenuto off the ledger line; no clef cut off.** Her 18:56 '혹시 다른 오류들 있나 한번 더 검사하고 넘어가자'. Swept the whole app (kit/qa448*.js, clefclip448.js, clefq448.js, fitall448.js): (1) answers: every drill level, 134 levels x 400 generated questions, the marked answer checked against the question: 0 problems. (2) notation: every level's questions mounted at 360px: every note head on a line or in a space, ledger lines where they belong (shared within a chord), nothing wider than the screen: the only real finding was ArticBar (Dynamics, articulation), whose dot and tenuto sat a whole space under the staff, where middle C's ledger line goes, so a tenuto read as a ledger line: patch448.py puts the dot and the tenuto half a space under the bottom line and points the wedge up at the note. (3) layout: every drill level at 390px, en and ko: no sideways scroll, no cut button text, no page errors. (4) clefs: since 447 put each clef on its line, a treble clef's tail hangs 1.68 spaces under the bottom line and several staves' boxes stopped short of it (the tail cut by up to a third of a space on paper: PaperStaff, SfStaff, BigStaff; a hair at the top of the curl in MelodyStaff and CurvePair; 0.3 units in KSStaff, PlaceIt, IntervalStaff, ChordStaff, StaffFrame, CutStaffSystem). patch448b.py: new clefInkYs(clef, yOf, st) = the clef's ink top and bottom from CLEF_GLYPH (0.6 of air); each of those boxes makes room for it. **A new staff with a clef: build its box with clefInkYs.** Measured on every drill page, every Lesson Book, Workbook and teacher page and the cut-outs (543 clefs) and in every drill level's questions: none cut off (before: 107 kinds). Three Workbook pages grew a few pixels and were tightened to fit (staff p6 'Clara visits' gaps, whole-staff p2 cell padding); all 124 printed books (en + ko) fit their A4 pages. The ledger-lines worksheet pictures remade (the guide drawings were already whole). Checks: lbcheck and wbcheck for chapters 6, 7, 11, 15 pass; sf405 22, ws419 45, ll444 82, tn444 16, ch3app397 35, ll431 24. |
"""
m = re.search(r'^\| 447 \| [^\n]*\n', s, re.M)
if not m: raise SystemExit('row 447')
s = s[:m.end()] + ROW + s[m.end():]
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s); print('CLAUDE.md: log row 448')
